## Project

FastAPI + PostgreSQL backend for a weekly meal planning assistant. A provider-agnostic AI client layer (Python ABC) drives recipe generation and chat refinement. No frontend — pure JSON API.

## Cross-cutting conventions (source of truth: docs/plans/_conventions.md)

Shared decisions that span domains live once in [`docs/plans/_conventions.md`](../../docs/plans/_conventions.md), each with a stable ID. The rules below and the domain plans reference them by ID rather than restating — when a shared decision changes, edit it there, not in each rule:

- `CONV-AUTH-OWNERSHIP` — per-user data isolation, 404-not-403 (see security.mdc, database.mdc)
- `CONV-AI-CLIENT-INJECTION` — provider abstraction + no-content logging (see ai-integration.mdc, testing.mdc)
- `CONV-METRIC-SINGULAR` — singular ingredient/unit names, metric quantities (see ai-integration.mdc)
- `CONV-DELETE-CASCADE` — 204 + DB cascade + cascade test (see database.mdc)
- `CONV-SUMMARY-SCHEMA` / `CONV-PAGINATION` — list-endpoint response shape + paging (see schemas.mdc)
- `CONV-CATEGORY-ENUM` — canonical ingredient/grocery categories
- `CONV-INGREDIENT-MODEL` — canonical ingredient identity; preparation lives on the recipe association (see database.mdc)

## Documentation map (where a fact belongs)

Each doc answers one question, and a fact has **exactly one home** — everywhere else references it by link or `CONV-*` ID. Before writing a fact, check whether it already lives somewhere; if so, link instead of restating.

- **What the system *is*** — current data model, endpoints, data flow → [`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`](../../docs/ARCHITECTURE.md). Update it when the *built reality* changes; it is the source of truth for current shape, not for rules or plans.
- **A rule that spans domains** → a `CONV-*` in [`docs/plans/_conventions.md`](../../docs/plans/_conventions.md).
- **Work to do, and *why* an approach was chosen, in one domain** → that domain's [`docs/plans/*.plan.md`](../../docs/plans) (`todos:` frontmatter = live status; body = rationale).
- **How to write code in this repo** → the `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` files (imperative, code-level enforcement of the above).

A plan must never be the *only* place a current fact lives — if it is, that fact belongs in ARCHITECTURE.md or a `CONV-*`. Truth flows toward ARCHITECTURE + conventions + code; plans hold work and rationale, then go quiet once their domain is built.

## Conventions & plan governance

- Reference `_conventions.md` rules by their `CONV-*` ID. **Never edit `_conventions.md` as a side effect** of another task.
- If a change would contradict a `CONV-*`, **stop and ask** whether to change the convention or the code — do not silently reconcile either side. A convention change is its own dedicated change and must update every plan that references the ID (and the counterpart `react-meal-planner-client` repo when the decision is shared, e.g. categories, metric units, summary/detail split).
- When a request adds a capability or changes the approach relative to the relevant `docs/plans/*.plan.md`, update that plan's `todos:` frontmatter **as part of the task** — a new `todos:` entry for new work, or a deviation note on the affected todo. Skip this for trivial one-offs (renames, small refactors) that don't change scope or decisions.

## Stack (source of truth: pyproject.toml)

- Python 3.12
- fastapi==0.135.1, uvicorn>=0.41.0
- SQLAlchemy>=2.0.36 (2.0 style ORM), alembic>=1.18.4
- psycopg[binary]>=3.3.3 (psycopg3 — NOT psycopg2 syntax)
- pydantic[email]==2.12+, pydantic-settings==2.13+
- passlib==1.7.4, python-jose==3.3.0, bcrypt 4.x (bcrypt backend), httpx, itsdangerous
- anthropic SDK (add via `uv add anthropic` when implementing AI layer)
- pytest (add via `uv add --dev pytest` when writing tests)

## Directory layout (do not deviate)

```
app/
  main.py          # app factory (create_app), router registration, lifespan
  config.py        # Settings via pydantic-settings; access via get_settings()
  core/
    deps.py        # get_current_user dependency
    security.py    # JWT encode/decode, password hashing
  db/
    base_class.py  # declarative Base
    base.py        # Base + all model imports (for Alembic env.py)
    session.py     # engine, SessionLocal, get_db dependency
  models/          # SQLAlchemy models: chat, grocery, ingredient, meal_plan, nutrition, recipe, user
  schemas/         # Pydantic v2 schemas
  routers/         # auth, chat, grocery, meal_plans, recipes, users
  services/        # recipe_service, chat_service, grocery_service, ingredient_service, nutrition_service, google_oidc, token_revocation
  clients/
    base.py               # ABC defining generate_recipes / chat_modify contract
    anthropic_client.py   # Anthropic concrete implementation
    fake.py               # recording test double — no real API calls
  utils/
    prompt_templates.py  # all prompt strings live here, nowhere else
alembic/           # migrations only — no business logic
```

## Build order

1. `setup-fastapi-project` — skeleton, config, health endpoint ✅
2. `db-and-models` — SQLAlchemy models + Alembic env ✅
3. `schemas-and-routers` — Pydantic schemas + router stubs ✅
4. `ai-provider-integration` — ABC + clients + prompt templates + services ✅
5. `grocery-and-nutrition-services` — grocery service extracted ✅; nutrition service (USDA) pending
6. Per-feature plans in `docs/plans/` are now the source of truth for remaining work

## Comments and Docstrings
- Do not add docstrings to classes or functions whose name and signature are self-explanatory
- Docstrings are appropriate when behavior, side effects, or parameters are non-obvious
- Do not add module-level docstrings
- Do not add inline comments that restate what the code does
- The developer will add comments where they deem necessary

## Documentation protocol

- **Auto-Update:** After feature completion, sync `/docs/` (ARCHITECTURE.md, DEPLOYMENT.md, SETUP.md, etc.) to match the new code.
- **New Dependencies:** If adding packages via `uv add`, update:
  - [docs/SETUP.md](docs/SETUP.md) — add to `.env` template if new env vars required
  - [README.md](README.md) — update tech stack section if it's a major dependency
- **Plans:** Update `docs/plans/*.plan.md` as you work (not only on completion) — mark tasks done, add a `todos:` entry for new work, and note deviations. See "Conventions & plan governance" above for scope.

## Do not

- Do not add packages not in `pyproject.toml` without explicit instruction (`uv add <package>` to add).
- Do not put business logic in routers or prompt strings outside `prompt_templates.py`.
- Do not use `text()` raw SQL — use ORM queries.
- Do not call the AI provider directly from routers or models.
- Do not add dependencies, refactoring, or "improvements" beyond what is asked.
- Do not modify `CLAUDE.md` or `.cursorrules` without explicit user permission.
